+//! Issue #651 (slice 4 of 6 of the #635 re-slicing, 0016 decisions 7(e)/(f)): **the passes
+//! that repair, move or rewrite a chunk map go through the shared resolver, under the same
+//! per-object containment — and a repoint is safe to persist.**
+//!
+//! Every leg drives the real entry points — [`reconcile_step`] (the fenced control point),
+//! [`reconcile_after_restore`], `backfill::reconcile` — never a parallel test-only path, and
+//! never the patch's own helpers: this file names no symbol the fix adds, so it is an
+//! **assertion** red on the pre-fix tree rather than a compile red.
+//!
+//! The fixture seeds **raw** `seg:` records plus a segmented root (this slice lands no
+//! producer of segmented maps; #653 owns the staged-publication committer), built with the
+//! real validating constructors so a fixture typo cannot silently change which rule a leg
+//! exercises.
+//!
+//! 1. `stranded_marked_is_zero_over_segmented_objects_while_real_garbage_is_still_marked` —
+//!    criterion (1): post-restore reconciliation never strands a segmented object's
+//!    fragments, and still marks genuinely unreferenced ones (so "0" is a verdict, not
+//!    silence).
+//! 2. `reconstruction_repairs_a_chunk_whose_chunkref_lives_in_a_segmented_record` and
+//!    `rebalance_evacuates_a_segmented_chunk_off_a_draining_server` — criterion (2): the
+//!    obligation is repaired rather than drained as unreferenced, the evacuation converges,
+//!    and each move's destination is **adopted** (its pre-mark deleted) while the vacated
+//!    source is **evidenced**.
+//! 3. `a_repoint_that_would_grow_a_record_past_the_value_ceiling_is_refused_not_persisted` —
+//!    criterion (2)'s ceiling half, over a record that is **legal before the move** and
+//!    would cross the ceiling **because of it**.
+//! 4. `backfill_leaves_a_segmented_record_byte_identical_while_filling_a_flat_one` —
+//!    criterion (3).
+//! 5. `reconstruction_resolves_each_objects_root_once_per_pass_not_once_per_queued_chunk` —
+//!    criterion (4), counted on an instrumented store.
+//! 6. `a_damaged_object_does_not_starve_the_healthy_ones_and_its_obligation_stays_queued`
+//!    and `a_drain_still_evacuates_the_servers_a_damaged_object_has_nothing_to_do_with` —
+//!    the per-object containment legs.
+
+#![forbid(unsafe_code)]
+
+use std::collections::HashMap;
+use std::sync::atomic::{AtomicUsize, Ordering};
+use std::sync::Mutex;
+
+use async_trait::async_trait;
+use bytes::Bytes;
+use wyrd_coordination_mem::MemCoordination;
+use wyrd_core::metadata::{
+    self, ChunkMap, ChunkRef, EcScheme, InodeId, InodeRecord, InodeState, SegmentGroup,
+    SegmentRecord, SegmentRef, SegmentedMap, MAX_VALUE_BYTES,
+};
+use wyrd_core::placement::Topology;
+use wyrd_core::write::encode_ec_fragment;
+use wyrd_core::{erasure, repair};
+use wyrd_custodian::backfill::reconcile as backfill_reconcile;
+use wyrd_custodian::desired_state::{set_lifecycle, DServerLifecycle};
+use wyrd_custodian::{
+    reconcile_after_restore, reconcile_step, BackfillContext, Custodian, ExpiredPendingPolicy,
+    FencedZone, GcContext, RebalanceContext, Reconciled, ReconstructionContext, RestoreReport,
+};
